WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.089
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.089 --> 00:00:04.880
So I'm back on the set of the Paper Towns
movie, but over the last, like, 100 hours,

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:10.090
you and me and the Katherine and both of our
parents, uh, had norovirus, which is a virus

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:11.750
with this amazing superpower.

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:16.510
It can make a human being stay on or near
a toilet for, like, 12 to 24 hours.

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:19.020
Side-note, Hank: Why don't fictional characters
ever get sick?

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:23.160
Like why is Captain Ahab never like "Uuuh,
god, I've got the worst head cold and my throat

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:28.200
is very scratchy and I just want to stay in
my bunk but if I don't get up and try to find

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.750
the white whale, human beings will never learn
about nature's complete indifference to them,

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:34.690
so I guess I'll go to work."?

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:39.280
Anyway, while I was horrifically ill, I kept
on wondering who exactly was responsible for

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:40.280
my norovirus.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:44.500
The thing is, Hank, you get norovirus almost
all the time by eating the poop of someone

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:45.550
who already has it.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:50.600
Now, you only have to eat, like, .00001 grams
in order to get norovirus, but it is - I,

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.309
I want to emphasize this: someone else's poop.

00:00:53.309 --> 00:00:57.180
Now, the clear Patient Zero in our family
is my daughter Alice; five days before Thanksgiving

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:01.460
she awoke from a nap and promptly vomited
all over her father, but I didn't get sick

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:02.460
then.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:05.790
I mention this only because it leads to the
uncomfortable awareness that in all likelihood,

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:09.639
all of us have eaten the poop of everyone
we love.

00:01:09.639 --> 00:01:12.009
I guess except if it's an Internet relationship.

00:01:12.009 --> 00:01:13.850
Man, Internet friendships are the best!

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:16.939
The next time someone says to me, like "Oh,
your Internet friendships aren't real," I'll

00:01:16.939 --> 00:01:21.819
be like, "Listen, if your construction of
reality involves necessarily eating poop,

00:01:21.819 --> 00:01:24.789
then I'm going to stay right here in my land
of fiction."

00:01:24.789 --> 00:01:28.459
Anyway, this poop eating business is great
stuff to think about when you're already extremely

00:01:28.459 --> 00:01:32.549
queasy from norovirus, but the other thing
I kept thinking is that my beautiful one-year-old

00:01:32.549 --> 00:01:37.139
daughter whose poop had started this whole
Thanksgiving family catastrophe was going

00:01:37.139 --> 00:01:38.139
to be OK.

00:01:38.139 --> 00:01:41.880
Like, norovirus is almost never fatal in kids
in the U.S., but around the world, it causes

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.569
more than 200,000 child deaths per year.

00:01:44.569 --> 00:01:48.520
And most of those kids die for want of clean
water and oral re-hydration solution that

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:50.289
costs, like, 50 cents.

00:01:50.289 --> 00:01:55.770
Alice got PediaLyte, that's the only difference
between, "Haha, what a funny family Thanksgiving

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:58.979
story," and the greatest personal disaster
I can imagine.

00:01:58.979 --> 00:02:02.349
And whatever Alice grows up to do - whatever
any of us grow up to do - let's remember all

00:02:02.349 --> 00:02:08.200
those times that everything rested on 50 cents
of PediaLyte or refrigerated penicillin or

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.229
access to clean water.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:12.920
Now, of course, the actual process of getting
oral re-hydration solutions to the kids who

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:17.690
need it is, like everything else in global
health and poverty, fiendishly complicated,

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:21.920
but I don't think we should let that complexity
stand in our way or intimidate us.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:25.480
Yes, it is hard, and yes, there are failures,
but organizations from Save the Children to

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:30.269
Water.org to countless local charities are
helping to decrease child mortality.

00:02:30.269 --> 00:02:33.849
Hank, I am in no way grateful for my brush
with norovirus, but it's helpful to think

00:02:33.849 --> 00:02:35.879
about as we head into Project for Awesome
season.

00:02:35.879 --> 00:02:40.609
The world is a profoundly unjust place; it
always has been and I imagine it always will

00:02:40.609 --> 00:02:45.409
be, but that doesn't absolve us of our responsibility
to look directly at problems even when they

00:02:45.409 --> 00:02:49.609
are painful to look at and to try our best
to do something to decrease world suck.

00:02:49.609 --> 00:02:53.590
So Hank: I'm sorry that you ate Alice's poop,
or possibly my poop; somebody's poop, anyway.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:57.250
But here's to the hope of getting better,
both individually and as a species.

00:02:57.250 --> 00:02:59.920
Hank, I'll see you on Friday.

